    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Lagrange&#x27;s mechanics lives in a &quot;position and velocity&quot; space (q, qdot); Hamilton&#x27;s 1834 reformulation trades each qdot for its canonically conjugate momentum p = dL/dqdot via a Legendre transform, and rewrites the second-order Euler-Lagrange equation as twice as many first-order equations for (q, p) moving through a single unified phase space:">

